EXCEPTION — VERB CONJUGATION TABLES (data-verbos.js)
----------------------------------------------------

The verb conjugation tables contained in data-verbos.js (the object
VERBOS: inflected forms and stress marks) are derived from data published
by OpenRussian.org (https://github.com/Badestrand/russian-dictionary),
licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
International License (CC BY-SA 4.0), and were cross-checked against the
pymorphy3 morphological analyzer (OpenCorpora dictionary, CC BY-SA).

In accordance with the ShareAlike condition, those conjugation tables are
distributed under CC BY-SA 4.0, not under CC BY-NC-ND 4.0:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

Changes made: selection of the verbs present in the AZBUKA lexicon,
correction of errors, choice among stress variants, removal of unused
forms, and conversion to AZBUKA's data format.

The usage notes ("nota") and all other original content in data-verbos.js
remain under CC BY-NC-ND 4.0, like the rest of this repository. The
case-government guide now lives in data-gramatica.js (GRAMATICA_RECCION),
which is original content under CC BY-NC-ND 4.0.

EXCEPTION — DECLENSION TABLES (data-casos.js)
---------------------------------------------

The declension tables contained in data-casos.js (the object CASOS:
inflected forms, stress marks, locative and partitive forms, and short
forms of adjectives) are derived from data published by OpenRussian.org
(https://github.com/Badestrand/russian-dictionary), licensed under the
Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License
(CC BY-SA 4.0). They were cross-checked against the pymorphy3
morphological analyzer (OpenCorpora dictionary, CC BY-SA) and against the
stress indexes of A. A. Zaliznyak's Grammatical Dictionary of Russian.

In accordance with the ShareAlike condition, those declension tables are
distributed under CC BY-SA 4.0, not under CC BY-NC-ND 4.0:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

Changes made: selection of the words present in the AZBUKA lexicon,
correction of stress and spelling errors, forms generated by rule for
regular adjectives, hand-written paradigms for pronouns and numerals,
selection of locative and partitive forms, and conversion to AZBUKA's
data format.

The usage notes ("nota") in data-casos.js, and the grammar explanations in
data-gramatica.js, are original content under CC BY-NC-ND 4.0, like the
rest of this repository.

EXCEPTION — SPANISH FREQUENCY DATA (data-lexicon-es.js)
-------------------------------------------------------

In the ABECÉ lexicon (data-lexicon-es.js, object LEXICON_ES), the
"sourceRefs" field of each entry holds frequency figures, lemmas and
categories taken from:

- the OpenSubtitles 2018 frequency list by Hermit Dave
  (https://github.com/hermitdave/FrequencyWords), CC BY-SA 4.0;
- CORPES XXI, Real Academia Española (frequency list, CC BY-SA 4.0), also
  kept as the source file herramientas/fuentes/diccionario_frecuencias_corpes_alfa.zip;
- wordfreq by Robyn Speer (https://github.com/rspeer/wordfreq), CC BY-SA 4.0.

In accordance with the ShareAlike condition, those data (the "sourceRefs"
fields and the CORPES source file) are distributed under CC BY-SA 4.0:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

Changes made: selection of the words in the ABECÉ lexicon and conversion to
its data format. Everything else in data-lexicon-es.js (translations,
definitions, examples, pronunciation, unit assignments) is original content
under CC BY-NC-ND 4.0. The Spanish–Russian dictionaries of WikDict and
FreeDict (CC BY-SA) were used only for comparison; no translation was copied.
The Spanish conjugations (data-verbos-es.js) are generated by rule
(herramientas/abece/conjugador-es.py) and were cross-checked against Fred
Jehle's Conjugated Spanish Verb Database and verbecc without copying forms.

